---
import BaseLayout from "../layouts/BaseLayout.astro";
---

<BaseLayout
  title="About"
  description="Why this studio exists, and why the sentences are written by hand."
  current="about"
>
  <article class="essay">
    <aside class="essay-rail">
      <span>Starter draft</span>
      <a href="/thoughts">Read thoughts</a>
    </aside>
    <div>
      <h1 class="essay-title">About</h1>
      <p class="essay-lede">
        A place to think out loud, and to keep the thoughts that would otherwise
        disappear.
      </p>
      <div class="prose">
        <p>
          This is not a software project. It is a writing studio I have wanted for a
          long time: a public room for the innermost work of paying attention. I do
          not want an audience in the ordinary sense. I want the quieter reward —
          that somewhere, someone shares a feeling I thought I was carrying alone.
        </p>
        <p>
          I remember a time, in high school, when reading and reflection were a
          daily practice. I wrote every sentence myself. Other people could help,
          but the agency stayed with me. I owned what I put down. In the years
          since, that habit thinned. In this era, almost everything on the
          internet is drafted or dressed by a model. I have a particular regard
          for the people who still sit with a blank page and refuse that shortcut.
        </p>
        <p>
          Dictation will bring the raw material in — on a commute, at the gym,
          wherever a thought arrives before it can be lost. A ring, a phone, a
          transcript: useful, and also incomplete. Speech is sparse, circular,
          sometimes illogical. It is not yet a paragraph. The work of this site is
          the second pass: turning that weather into sentences that can be lived
          with, and understood only by living.
        </p>
        <p>
          The process is not only for other people. It is how I come to understand
          myself. Nothing here is polished by a machine in my name. If a sentence
          is published, I have stood in it.
        </p>
        <p>
          <em>This page is a starter. Rewrite it until it sounds like you.</em>
        </p>
      </div>
    </div>
  </article>
</BaseLayout>
